  "id": "Compound::DB01192 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Oxymorphone is associated with Cyp2d6 through multiple pathways involving opioid agonists. Oxymorphone, as part of the Full Opioid Agonists class, binds to Cyp2d6 through interactions with Dextropropoxyphene and Dihydrocodeine, both of which are also included in this class. These compounds are known to interact with the cytochrome P450 2D6 enzyme, which is involved in the metabolism of various drugs. The presence of multiple pathways linking Oxymorphone to Cyp2d6 indicates a potential role in drug metabolism, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence is supported by the shared lowest common ancestors in the pathways, suggesting a common functional or structural relationship between the entities. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in the association, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the biological relevance of these interactions.",
